<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  doctrine: doctorcre-v5-design-basis

  com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep: daily V5-A05 delivery-cadence sweep.

  A LAUNCH AGENT, NOT A SCHEDULED MODEL SESSION (PROP-010's ruling; see
  com.carr.timebomb-audit.plist's own header). Reading cadence-status and,
  only on a detected miss, calling raise-delivery-cadence-alert is a fixed
  predicate pipeline over deterministic record-layer reads and one bounded
  write, not a judgement call about what to do next.

  07:00 local: before the working day starts, so a miss detected overnight is
  already in the morning brief's assurance_cadence section when Joe or Dell
  first opens it.

  RISK: YELLOW. Read-only against ops.v5_a05_cadence_receipt via the
  cadence-status verb for every run; on a detected miss (status: "missed"),
  writes exactly one raise-delivery-cadence-alert call per subject, idempotent
  per (subject, expiry instant) via a deterministic uuid5 key, so a second run
  before the miss is resolved is a no-op duplicate rather than a repeat alert.
  Never issues a cadence receipt itself (that stays a human/process action);
  never touches any other record-layer surface.

  See ops/delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.py's own header for the full pipeline and its
  bounded v1 subject scope.

  INSTALLING IT IS A DELIBERATE HUMAN ACT, and there is no installer script on
  purpose: a bin/install-*.sh is an external-admin ingress that would need its
  own SCAC registry successor. From the canonical checkout:
    sed "s|{{REPO}}|$PWD|g" ops/launchd/com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.plist \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.plist
    plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.plist
  Once installed, ops/config-as-code.py check holds the installed body to
  this file like every other CARR LaunchAgent.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.carr.delivery-cadence-a05-sweep</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/run-scheduled.sh</string>
    <string>delivery-cadence-a05-sweep</string>
    <string>launchd.run</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/ops/delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>CARR_REPO</key>
    <string>{{REPO}}</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/delivery-cadence-a05-sweep.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
